In `faker/generator.py`, `parse(text)` returns `_re_token.sub(self.__format_token, text)`, so each regex match for a `{{ ... }}` token invokes `__format_token` once. In `__format_token`, there is exactly one `self.format(...)` call per token, regardless of whether the token uses an argument group. The test template in `files/testcase.py` contains eight tokens total, so one `parse` call produces eight calls to `Generator.format`.

